                <pb facs="0748" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6843: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-12-12T20:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12,
                                1925—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 13—11:15
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>527. My 524, December 11, 7 p.m. International train arrived Peking at 6 this
                    evening with all on board unhurt and well.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
